<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shimane Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shimane Prefecture is a prefecture in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chugoku-region">Chūgoku region</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsue">Matsue</a>. It covers the old provinces of Izumo, Iwami and Oki, and includes the ancient shrine of Izumo Taisha and the Iwami Ginzan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mine. It was created after the abolition of the domains in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shimane-prefecture.jpg" alt="Shimane Prefecture" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MaedaAkihiko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Izumo-Taisha_Haiden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
